 -- root <jens@proknx.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200

aragon-ai (1.5.31) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed searxng-mcp.service using a resident `uvx` wrapper, which held
    a permanent lock on ~/.cache/uv/.lock and blocked `uv cache clean`
    in monthly-disk-cleanup.sh (0 MB freed every run, traced via
    uv-lock-diagnose.sh). install_searxng() now runs `uv tool install`
    at install time; ExecStart points directly at the pinned binary.

 -- root <jens@proknx.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200

aragon-ai (1.5.30) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed chat UI serving a cold KV-cache while the voice path serves the
    same request warm. Root cause: searxng-mcp-proxy.py (port 8092) used
    the stock single-threaded http.server.HTTPServer, so it can only
    handle one request at a time; any request arriving while a prior one
    is still in flight (e.g. blocked on the upstream urlopen(...,
    timeout=30) call to searxng-mcp-server) just queues with no response.
    llama-server's --ui-mcp-proxy live per-turn MCP fetch enforces a much
    shorter client-side timeout than that, so a queued request gets
    cancelled ("MCP error -32001: Request timed out") well before the
    proxy would ever reply. That silently dropped all 5 SearXNG tools
    from that turn's tools array, which changed the rendered prompt just
    enough to invalidate the entire cached KV prefix (170s cold vs 21s
    warm for an otherwise identical request). aragon_agent.py's
    curl/voice path never hit this because it fetches tools once at
    startup and caches them, so it was never exposed to a busy proxy.
    Fixed by switching searxng-mcp-proxy.py to
    http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer so concurrent requests no longer
    serialize.

 -- root <jens@proknx.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 09:45:00 +0200

aragon-ai (1.5.29) stable; urgency=high

  * Fixed 1.5.28's git-prompt fix not actually taking effect for the
    SearXNG source clone/re-pin: those git calls run via
    `sudo -H -u searxng git ...`, and sudo resets the environment by
    default, dropping GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT/GIT_ASKPASS before they reach
    git even though the script exports them. A fresh install on
    2026-09-03 still hung on "Username for 'https://github.com':" during
    the initial SearXNG clone, confirming this. The two SearXNG git
    calls that touch the network (clone, fetch) now set
    GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 and GIT_ASKPASS=/bin/true explicitly via `env`
    on the sudo'd command itself, which isn't subject to sudo's
    environment filtering. The node-sonos-http-api re-pin step already
    worked correctly since it doesn't go through sudo.

 -- root <jens@proknx.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 08:59:00 +0200

aragon-ai (1.5.28) stable; urgency=high

  * Fixed installer (postinst) hanging indefinitely during upgrade/install:
    the SearXNG source re-pin step (and the node-sonos-http-api re-pin step)
    run `git fetch`/`git clone` over the network, and git's own credential
    prompt writes straight to the controlling terminal, bypassing the
    script's stdout/stderr redirection. Under the unattended gotty install
    terminal, that prompt has nobody to answer it, so the install hung
    forever on "Username for 'https://github.com':" instead of failing into
    the warn-and-continue / rollback handling already written for these
    steps. Fixed by disabling git's interactive credential prompt for the
    whole script (`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, `GIT_ASKPASS=/bin/true`), so a
    git step that can't authenticate now fails fast and visibly instead of
    blocking the install.

