    without a fixed version — Home Assistant rules, the Spotify voice
    module, the search engine itself, the Sonos integration, and the core
    agent and voice-tool services. All of these now install the exact,
    tested version every time, including on a routine update to an
    already-running device, so a change on the internet can no longer
    silently break something that worked yesterday.

