aragon-ai (1.5.23) stable; urgency=low

  * Fixed the KV-cache warm-up so the chat/voice assistant is actually ready
    when the web UI says it is. Two separate bugs could leave the very
    first request after a reboot or restart taking 1-2 minutes instead of
    being instant: an unused, unbuilt "/report" feature was silently
    evicting the just-warmed chat cache right after warm-up finished, and
    a stray trailing newline in the prompt file made the warm-up's cached
    prompt not match what the browser/voice pipeline actually sends.

  * Fixed unit conversion rejecting spoken unit names it should have
    understood — e.g. "convert fifty centilitres into millilitres" or
    "convert 100 yards into centimeters" — because only abbreviations
    (cm, mm, mg, cl, ml, hPa) were recognized, not the full spoken words.

  * Fixed a misleading "the request timed out" answer for some unit
    conversions and other multi-step requests. The assistant now clearly
    logs when it genuinely ran out of attempts instead of hitting an
    actual timeout, and the calculator's supported units are now fully
    documented so it converges in fewer attempts to begin with.

  * Fixed the assistant sometimes calculating math itself instead of
    using the calculator tool, which could produce a wrong answer for
    anything beyond simple arithmetic (e.g. expressions combining square
    roots and pi).

  * Fixed "how many days until X" questions sometimes returning a wrong
    number of days — the assistant no longer needs to guess today's date
    itself.

  * Fixed currency conversion answers reading currency codes as letters
    ("E U R") instead of names ("Euros").

  * Fixed weather answers giving an inconsistent or misspelled
    temperature unit, and vague weather questions ("what's the weather",
    "this week") sometimes answering for the wrong city instead of the
    device's home location.

  * Fixed voice answers sometimes including raw web links or markdown
    formatting, which don't make sense read aloud.

  * News search ("top news", "what's happening in X") no longer has a
    single point of failure: Google News was added alongside Bing News,
    so a Bing page-layout change can no longer take news search down
    entirely. Search results were also trimmed to reduce voice response
    time.

