    after install/upgrade (dependency installation, KV-cache warm-up):
    it could be killed before finishing — sometimes before the Spotify
    voice cache was warmed, and before some routine end-of-setup
    maintenance ran — due to two unrelated timing issues. The two
    cache warm-ups (chat and Spotify) now run one after the other
    instead of racing each other for the same CPU, and the step no
    longer terminates itself while finishing up.

